  "foaf:name": "Centinela I Community &amp; Action from Southern Seas",
  "sdo:name": "Centinela I Community &amp; Action from Southern Seas",
  "sdo:description": "The Centinela I is the first university-operated sail training vessel in Chile dedicated to advancing ocean culture, science, and community engagement from the Southern Hemisphere. Operating across southern Chile, remote islands, and the South Pacific, it serves as a mobile platform for interdisciplinary scientific expeditions, academic training, and outreach in isolated coastal and insular communities. The project fosters the next generation of ocean leaders through hands-on experiences, contributes new scientific data on remote marine ecosystems, and strengthens resilience in vulnerable communities. By bridging science, education, and local knowledge, Centinela I positions Chile as a key contributor to the Ocean Decade, promoting global collaboration, sustainability, and a deeper cultural connection with the ocean.",
